      "created_at": "2016-10-21T08:50:32Z",
      "updated_at": "2016-10-21T08:50:32Z",
      "body": "Thanks @fhanik for the fix.\nHowever, I am wondering if it would not make more sense to use a more standard claim such as [\"sub\"](http://openid.net/specs/openid-connect-core-1_0.html#SubjectIDTypes) to represent user id instead of the non standard \"user_id\" claim.\n",
